  "@context": {
    "@base": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/",
    "@vocab": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#",
    "dcterms": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/",
    "adms": "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#",
    "schema": "https://schema.org/",
    "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#",
    "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
    "skos": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#",
    "xsd": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#",
    "owl": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#",
    "m3": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/M3_GenesisGrammar.jsonld#"
  },
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:GrammarFoundation",
      "@type": "owl:Ontology",
      "owl:versionInfo": "2.10.0",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-05-12",
      "dcterms:modified": "2026-09-30",
      "dcterms:creator": "Echopraxium with the collaboration of Claude AI",
      "dcterms:title": "TSCG M3 Grammar Foundation",
      "dcterms:description": "Apex ontology of the TSCG hierarchy — no imports, no dependencies. Defines the Lambek Calculus mathematical foundation (free commutative monoidal categories), the six indexed operators (×, +, |), abstract classes M3Grammar and MonoidalType, the TSCG type system hierarchy (𝕋₀→𝕄₀), and the intersubjective benchmark properties. Imported by M3_EagleEye, M3_SphinxEye, and M3_GenesisGrammar.",
      "rdfs:label": "M3 Grammar Foundation — TSCG Apex Ontology",
      "rdfs:comment": "Foundational definitions for the TSCG Structural Grammar. Rooted in Lambek Calculus (Lambek 1958) and free commutative monoidal categories (MacLane 1963). The ⊗ operator is a monoidal product — NOT an algebraic tensor product. No metric, no Hilbert space, no scalar multiplication required or assumed.",
      "metadata": {
        "layer": "M3",
        "name": "Grammar Foundation",
        "version": "2.2.0",
        "architecture": "apex — no owl:imports",
        "date_created": "2026-05-12",
        "date_modified": "2026-05-27",
        "authors": [
          "Echopraxium with the collaboration of Claude AI"
        ],
        "imported_by": [
          "M3_EagleEye.jsonld",
          "M3_SphinxEye.jsonld",
          "M3_GenesisGrammar.jsonld"
        ],
        "changelog": {
          "v1.1.0": "MAJOR UPDATE: Added dcterms metadata, skos namespace. Fixed owl:versionInfo prefix. Added 6 indexed operators (⊗ᵗ, ⊗ᵐ, Fm2, Fm2, _^ / _$, _^ / _$). Added type system hierarchy (𝕋₀/𝕋₁/𝕋₂/𝕄₀). Added m3:grammar_foundation:intersubjectiveBenchmark and m3:grammar_foundation:defeasibilityStatus. Confirmed apex position: no owl:imports.",
          "v1.0.0": "Initial skeleton: M3Grammar and M3Dimension abstract classes, grammarType and monoidalProduct properties."
        }
      },
      "mathematical_foundation": {
        "formalism": "Lambek Calculus / Free Commutative Monoidal Categories",
        "references": [
          "Lambek, J. (1958). The mathematics of sentence structure. American Mathematical Monthly 65(3): 154-170.",
          "MacLane, S. (1963). Natural associativity and commutativity. Rice University Studies.",
          "MacLane, S. (1971). Categories for the Working Mathematician. Springer."
        ],
        "operator_disclaimer": "⊗ shares notation with the algebraic tensor product but operates in a distinct context: a typed combinatorial grammar without metric structure. Analogous to how × denotes both scalar multiplication and vector cross product — same symbol, different mathematical contexts.",
        "see_also": "ontology/StructuralGrammar/TSCG_StructuralGrammar_as_Mathematical_Foundation_README.md"
      },
      "m3:changelog": [
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.10.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-09-30",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1h: explicit local declarations of every external term used in the canonical corpus (principle, Michel: everything RDF-interpretable, no implicit term). Declared here, in the apex, with OWL type and rdfs:isDefinedBy: 6 OWL 2 built-in annotation properties (rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, rdfs:isDefinedBy, owl:versionInfo, owl:deprecated), 10 DCMI terms, 15 SKOS terms (official SKOS typing: ObjectProperty relations, skos:related symmetric, skos:notation DatatypeProperty, AnnotationProperty notes/labels, skos:Concept / skos:ConceptScheme classes, official subPropertyOf links among used terms), adms:versionNotes and schema:value. schema.org ACCEPTED as an external vocabulary where it fills a DCMI/SKOS gap (Michel, 2026-09-30); prefix schema declared. New node m3:grammar_foundation:ExternalVocabularyPolicy records the rules: declare once in the apex, never owl:imports external vocabularies, never declare the OWL 2 reserved axiom vocabulary (OWL 2 Structural Specification §5.1-§5.6 — it would leave OWL 2 DL). Not touched: this file's own @vocab (owl#) bare-key projections, left for B1/B2 and the vestiges lot (counted by the new gauge EXT-2). Triage: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-1/WS-1_FamilyA_Triage.md."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.9.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-09-30",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1g (Family A). Bare keys (dropped on JSON-LD expansion) replaced: alternative_names -> skos:altLabel, comment -> dcterms:description (consistent with lot 1b), note -> skos:note, definition -> skos:definition, label -> rdfs:label, title -> dcterms:title, id -> dcterms:identifier, rationale -> m3:rationale (declared in M3_GrammarFoundation, rdfs:subPropertyOf skos:note). In this file: label 4, note 2. Triage: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-1/WS-1_FamilyA_Triage.md. NEW: m3:rationale declared (owl:AnnotationProperty, rdfs:subPropertyOf skos:note) — no standard vocabulary offers a rationale/justification property (Michel, 2026-09-30)."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.8.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-09-30",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1c (Family A). Changelog entry keys, previously bare and dropped on JSON-LD expansion, replaced by standards: version -> owl:versionInfo, date -> dcterms:date, changes -> adms:versionNotes (ADMS: a description of changes between this version and the previous one). Prefix adms declared in @context: ADMS accepted as an external vocabulary (Michel, 2026-09-30). Changelog entries become graph-visible. Legacy changelog forms (maps keyed by version, metadata blocks) left for a separate lot. Triage: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-1/WS-1_FamilyA_Triage.md. The m3:changelog declaration records the decision in its skos:note (replaces the former 'pending a decision' wording)."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.7.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-09-30",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1b (Family A). Bare key 'description' (declared in no @context, hence dropped on JSON-LD expansion) replaced by the standard dcterms:description (DCMI: an account of the resource; literal). Chosen over rdfs:comment on semantic grounds (Michel, 2026-09-30). 6 occurrences. Side fix: under this file's @vocab (owl#) the bare key had minted the bogus term owl:description (6 triples); it is now dcterms:description. Bare 'description' inside legacy 'metadata' blocks left untouched (separate lot). No semantic change: documentation made graph-visible. Triage: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-1/WS-1_FamilyA_Triage.md."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.6.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-09-30",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1a (Family A). Bare keys 'examples' / 'example' (declared in no @context, hence dropped on JSON-LD expansion) replaced by the standard skos:example (SKOS documentation property, owl:AnnotationProperty, no domain/range): a list value now yields one skos:example triple per item. 1 list occurrence (3 examples). Side fix: under this file's @vocab (owl#) the bare key had minted the bogus term owl:examples; it is now skos:example. No semantic change: documentation made graph-visible. Triage: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-1/WS-1_FamilyA_Triage.md."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.5.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-07-22",
          "adms:versionNotes": "CHANGELOG PROPERTY DEFINED: new m3:changelog (owl:AnnotationProperty). The changelog property was used corpus-wide but DECLARED NOWHERE. It is defined here, in the apex ontology, so that every lower layer (M2/M1/M0 — all of which import M3) can use it as a legal downward reference. Also applied to this file: m2:changelog → m3:changelog, fixing both a dependency inversion (M3 referencing M2) and a CTX-1 defect (the 'm2' prefix was undeclared here). KNOWN LIMITS, deferred to the undeclared-terms worksite: (a) changelog entry objects still carry undeclared bare keys (version/date/changes) and remain invisible on expansion; (b) this file still declares @vocab=owl#, so its bare terms — including the legacy metadata.changelog block — expand into the OWL namespace as owl:* properties."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "2.4.1",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-07-18",
          "adms:versionNotes": "@context hygiene fix (CTX): 'm3' prefix made ABSOLUTE (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Echopraxium/tscg/main/ontology/M3_GenesisGrammar.jsonld#). It was relative and, combined with @vocab=owl#, resolved m3:* terms (incl. MonoidalType) against owl# instead of the M3 namespace — desynchronising this file's IRIs from EagleEye/SphinxEye. @base also repaired (.../main/ -> .../main/ontology/). Data graph unchanged."
        }
      ],
      "three_alphabets": {
        "dcterms:description": "Three primitive alphabets — one per monoidal operator.",
        "territory": {
          "notation": "𝕋₀(×) = {A, S, F, I, D}",
          "grammar": "Territory Grammar Gt — Eagle Eye",
          "operator": "×",
          "neutral": "m3:grammar_foundation:EmptyTerritory",
          "perspective": "What systems ARE"
        },
        "map": {
          "notation": "𝕋₀(+) = {R, E, V, O, Im}",
          "grammar": "Map Grammar Gm — Sphinx Eye",
          "operator": "+",
          "neutral": "m3:grammar_foundation:EmptyMap",
          "perspective": "How models QUALIFY"
        },
        "stereopsis": {
          "notation": "𝕋₀(|) = {T, _^, _$, K, Ss, L}  — symbolic notation only, not URIs",
          "grammar": "Stereopsis Grammar Gs — Bicephalous Perspective",
          "operator": "|",
          "neutral": "m3:grammar_foundation:StereopsisEmptySet",
          "perspective": "How Territory and Map CORRESPOND",
          "cardinality": 6,
          "asymmetry_note": "5-5-6 asymmetry: Gs has 6 primitives because the inter-grammar axis requires encoding convergence discrimination (L) that presupposes both Gt and Gm",
          "acronym": "TKSL — the 4 nominal Gs primitives (T=Temporality, K=Knowledge, Ss=Symbol, L=Localizability). Poles _^/_$ are polarity modifiers, not nominal primitives.",
          "transcendental_questions": {
            "T": "When?",
            "K": "What?",
            "Ss": "Sign?",
            "L": "Converging?"
          },
          "primitives_note": "T=Temporality, _^=PositivePole, _$=NegativePole, K=Knowledge, Ss=Symbol(Stereopsic), L=Localizability. Symbols _^/_$ are string notations only — OWL identifiers: m3:bicephalous:PositivePole, m3:bicephalous:NegativePole",
          "see_also": "M3_BicephalousPerspective.jsonld"
        }
      },
      "operator_grammar_types": {
        "dcterms:description": "× and + are intra-grammar (closed). | is inter-grammar (open). Explained within Lambek framework only.",
        "intra_grammar": {
          "territory_product": {
            "operator": "×",
            "domain": "Gt × Gt",
            "codomain": "Gt"
          },
          "map_sum": {
            "operator": "+",
            "domain": "Gm × Gm",
            "codomain": "Gm"
          }
        },
        "inter_grammar": {
          "stereopsic_fusion": {
            "operator": "|",
            "domain": "(Gt ∪ Gm ∪ Gs) × (Gt ∪ Gm ∪ Gs)",
            "codomain": "Gs",
            "associativity": "| is associative: (a | b) | c = a | (b | c)",
            "pole_pattern_positive": "expr_Territory | expr_Map | _^  (e.g. Coherence)",
            "pole_pattern_negative": "expr_Territory | expr_Map | _$  (e.g. Incoherence)",
            "precedence": "× > + > |  (highest to lowest)",
            "see_also": "ontology/docs/OntologyModeling_Guidelines.md Guideline 8"
          }
        }
      },
      "m2_functions_and_morphisms": {
        "skos:note": "Φ and Ψ are MORPHISMS (structure-preserving maps between grammars — they compose). Fm2 and Fm1m2 are FUNCTIONS, NOT morphisms and NOT functors: their essence is combination with emergence, which is non-compositional, whereas a morphism/functor must preserve composition. The two families are kept separate on purpose. See StructuralGrammar/Functional_Grammar_Model.md.",
        "dcterms:description": "Combination FUNCTIONS at M2/M1 level (Fm2, Fm1m2) alongside the genuine inter-grammar MORPHISMS (Φ, Ψ). Distinct from the monoidal operators ×/+/|, which act at 𝕋₀ on atoms. Fm2/Fm1m2 are functions, not morphisms: emergence is non-compositional.",
        "Fm2": {
          "signature": "Fm2 : GenericConcept²⁺ → GenericConceptCombo",
          "dcterms:description": "GenericConcept composition. Replaces former ⊗⇒ notation.",
          "example_1": "Fm2(Memory, Entropy) = Inertia",
          "example_2": "Fm2(Incoherence, Invariant) = TopologicalDefect",
          "example_3": "Fm2(Process, Step, Trajectory) = PipelineProcess",
          "kind": "function (not a morphism, not a functor) — emergence is non-compositional",
          "arity": "≥ 2 named concepts (M2_GenericConcepts or M1_CoreConcepts). Never primitives. Never joined by ×/+/|."
        },
        "Fm1m2": {
          "signature": "Fm1m2 : Domain⁺, GenericConcept⁺ → DomainConceptCombo",
          "dcterms:description": "KnowledgeField + GenericConcept composition.",
          "example_1": "Fm1m2(Biology, Process) = BiologicalProcess",
          "example_2": "Fm1m2(Physics, Coherence) = LaserCoherence",
          "kind": "function (not a morphism, not a functor) — emergence is non-compositional",
          "arity": "≥ 1 Domain AND ≥ 1 named concept. Domain QUALIFICATION is what distinguishes Fm1m2 from Fm2 — NOT 'crossing the M1/M2 boundary' (an Fm2 argument may itself come from M1_CoreConcepts)."
        },
        "family": "MORPHISMS: Φ (Gt→Gm), Ψ (Gm→Gt) — structure-preserving, they compose. FUNCTIONS: Fm2, Fm1m2 — emergence, non-compositional, they do NOT compose."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:M3Grammar",
      "@type": "owl:Class",
      "rdfs:label": "M3 Grammar (Abstract)",
      "rdfs:comment": "Abstract base class for M3-level structural grammars. Concrete subclasses: TerritoryGrammar (Gt, ASFID primitives) and MapGrammar (Gm, REVOI primitives).",
      "skos:definition": "A free commutative monoidal grammar over a finite set of primitive types. Characterized by: primitives (generators), monoidal operator (× for Gt, + for Gm, | for Gs), combination function (Fm2 — emergence, non-compositional), and pole primitives (_^ / _$)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:MonoidalType_base",
      "@type": "owl:Class",
      "rdfs:label": "Monoidal Type Base (formerly M3Dimension)",
      "rdfs:comment": "Abstract base class for M3 primitive types. At M2/M3: generators of structural formulas (qualitative, no metric). At M0: instantiation functors map structural primitives to observable instance values (quantitative scoring belongs to the M0 ValueSpace, not to the M3 structural grammar).",
      "skos:definition": "A primitive type in the TSCG Structural Grammar. Plays two roles: (1) generator of type expressions at M2 level; (2) evaluation functor at M0 level via norm-referenced scoring against intersubjective benchmarks.",
      "skos:note": "The word 'dimension' is used in the analytical sense (independent axis of characterisation), NOT in the metric/Hilbert sense."
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:grammarType",
      "@type": "owl:DatatypeProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "Grammar Type",
      "rdfs:comment": "Type of grammar — prevents collision between M3 structural grammar and M0 instance grammar (e.g. SHACL validation grammars).",
      "rdfs:domain": {
        "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:M3Grammar"
      },
      "rdfs:range": {
        "@id": "xsd:string"
      },
      "skos:example": "free_commutative_monoidal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:monoidalProduct",
      "@type": "owl:DatatypeProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "Monoidal Operators ×, +, |",
      "rdfs:comment": "Three free commutative monoidal operators of TSCG — one per grammar. × (Territory, intra-ASFID), + (Map, intra-REVOI), | (Stereopsis, inter-grammar). Replaces former single indexed form ⊗ⁱ.",
      "rdfs:domain": {
        "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:M3Grammar"
      },
      "rdfs:range": {
        "@id": "xsd:string"
      },
      "skos:definition": "The structural co-activation operator of the TSCG Concept Grammar. Encodes simultaneous presence of multiple primitive types in a concept signature.",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:axioms": {
        "territory_associativity": "(A × B) × C = A × (B × C)",
        "territory_commutativity": "A × B = B × A",
        "territory_neutral": "A × EmptyTerritory = A",
        "map_associativity": "(R + E) + V = R + (E + V)",
        "map_commutativity": "R + E = E + R",
        "map_neutral": "R + EmptyMap = R",
        "stereopsis_associativity": "(a | b) | c = a | (b | c)",
        "stereopsis_neutral": "x | StereopsisEmptySet = x",
        "no_metric": "no norm, no inner product, no scalar multiplication"
      },
      "m3:grammar_foundation:operatorForms": {
        "territory": "×  — Territory structural product (intra-Gt, closed within ASFID)",
        "map": "+  — Map structural sum (intra-Gm, closed within REVOI)",
        "stereopsis": "|  — Stereopsic fusion (inter-grammar, always produces Gs)"
      },
      "m3:grammar_foundation:precedence": "× > + > |  (highest to lowest binding strength)",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:associativity": "All three are associative and commutative",
      "skos:example": "D × It × F = Process  |  R + O = ModelQuality  |  A × S × It | R + O = Coherence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:dualityOperator",
      "@type": "owl:DatatypeProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "Pole Primitives _^ and _$  (replaces former ^op)",
      "rdfs:comment": "Stereopsis Grammar Gs primitives _^ (PositivePole) and _$ (NegativePole). Applied as: formula | _^  (positive pole)  or  formula | _$  (negative pole). Replaces former duality operator _^ / _$ (vestige of tensor algebra). Defined in M3_BicephalousPerspective.jsonld.",
      "rdfs:domain": {
        "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:M3Grammar"
      },
      "rdfs:range": {
        "@id": "xsd:string"
      },
      "skos:definition": "Dual type operator: maps a concept type to its structural opposite. Corresponds to negation in propositional logic via the Curry-Howard correspondence.",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:pole_forms": {
        "positive": "_^  — PositivePole — applied as: formula | _^",
        "negative": "_$  — NegativePole — applied as: formula | _$",
        "skos:note": "Both _^ and _$ are primitives of 𝕋₀(|) — string notations only, not URIs"
      },
      "skos:example": "A × S × It | R + O | _^  = Coherence  (positive pole)\nA × S × It | R + O | _$  = Incoherence  (negative pole)",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:positivePolePrimitive": "_^  — PositivePole — onset/amplifying pole of a GenericConcept pair",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:negativePolePrimitive": "_$  — NegativePole — terminus/attenuating pole of a GenericConcept pair"
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:TypeSystem",
      "@type": "owl:NamedIndividual",
      "rdfs:label": "TSCG Type System",
      "rdfs:comment": "Complete type hierarchy of the TSCG Structural Grammar across all layers.",
      "skos:definition": "Four-level type hierarchy derived from 10 primitive types via 3 operators.",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:levels": {
        "T0": {
          "rdfs:label": "Primitive Types",
          "notation": "𝕋₀ = 16 primitives (Base16): {A,St,F,It,D} ∪ {R,E,V,O,Im} ∪ {T,_^,_$,K,Ss,L}  (symbolic — _^ _$ are string notations)",
          "cardinality": 16,
          "layer": "M3",
          "role": "generators of the TSCG Structural Grammar",
          "acronyms": {
            "territory": "ASFID — Attractor, Structure, Flow, Information, Dynamics",
            "map": "REVOI — Representability, Evolvability, Verifiability, Observability, Interoperability",
            "stereopsis_nominal": "TKSL — Temporality, Knowledge, Symbol(Ss), Localizability",
            "stereopsis_poles": "_^/_$ — PositivePole / NegativePole (polarity modifiers)"
          },
          "subsets": {
            "territory": "{A, St, F, It, D} — 𝕋₀(×) Gt  (5 primitives — ASFID)",
            "map": "{R, E, V, O, Im} — 𝕋₀(+) Gm  (5 primitives — REVOI)",
            "stereopsis": "𝕋₀(|) Gs — 6 primitives: T (Temporality), _^ (PositivePole), _$ (NegativePole), K (Knowledge), Ss (Symbol/Stereopsic), L (Localizability)  [TKSL + poles]"
          },
          "notation_convention": "In hybrid formulas (containing |), Territory and Map types carry their monoid index: It (Information/Territory), St (Structure/Territory), O (Observability/Map). Pure intra-monoid formulas (A×S×F) and ASFID/REVOI scoring terminology are unaffected."
        },
        "T1": {
          "rdfs:label": "Derived Types (Named Product Types)",
          "notation": "𝕋₁ = { τ₁ OP τ₂ OP ... OP τₙ  |  τᵢ ∈ 𝕋₀,  OP ∈ {×, +, |} }",
          "layer": "M2",
          "role": "M2 GenericConcepts — named structural formulas",
          "skos:example": [
            "Process    = D × I × F",
            "Coherence  = A × S × It | R + O",
            "Entropy    = D × F | _$"
          ]
        },
        "T2": {
          "rdfs:label": "Compound Types (Emergent Combos)",
          "notation": "𝕋₂ = compositions of 𝕋₁ expressions via ×, +, |",
          "layer": "M1",
          "role": "M1 GenericConceptCombos — emergent compound concepts",
          "dcterms:description": "Higher-order types — complex compositions of 𝕋₁. Emergence operators (Fm2) were defined here but removed (no corpus usage). Composition of GenericConcepts is now expressed via the Fm2 and Fm1m2 FUNCTIONS (not morphisms — emergence is non-compositional)."
        },
        "M0": {
          "rdfs:label": "Terms (Proof Terms)",
          "notation": "𝕄₀ = { poclets inhabiting a type τ ∈ 𝕋₁ ∪ 𝕋₂ }",
          "layer": "M0",
          "role": "Instances that prove a system inhabits a conceptual type",
          "curry_howard": "Poclet = proof term. δ₁ = degree of proof (Curry-Howard correspondence)."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:intersubjectiveBenchmark",
      "@type": "owl:ObjectProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "Intersubjective Benchmark",
      "rdfs:comment": "Domain-contextualized canonical poclet(s) used as scoring reference for M0 instances. Grounds TSCG measurement in norm-referenced intersubjective consensus. Defeasible by design — valid until superseded by broader consensus.",
      "skos:definition": "A provisional structural attractor of a conceptual domain, identified by multi-cook convergence, domain-contextualized by default, explicitly defeasible, and self-improving through corpus growth.",
      "rdfs:range": {
        "@id": "xsd:string"
      },
      "m3:grammar_foundation:structure": {
        "epistemicScore": {
          "property": "m0:epistemicGap",
          "formula": "||ASFID_mean - REVOI_mean|| / sqrt(2)",
          "range": "[0.0, 1.0]"
        },
        "objectivityLevel": {
          "values": [
            "Subjective",
            "MultiExpertConsensus",
            "CanonCalibrated",
            "ContextualizedBenchmark"
          ],
          "default": "ContextualizedBenchmark"
        },
        "benchmarkRefs": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "uri": "IRI of canonical poclet",
            "domain": "M1 domain  (e.g. m1:Biology, m1:Electronics)",
            "canonType": "DomainSpecific | CrossDomain | Universal",
            "weight": "xsd:float  [0.0, 1.0]"
          }
        },
        "expertConsensus": {
          "numberOfExperts": "xsd:integer",
          "convergenceScore": "xsd:float  (ICC / Cohen kappa)",
          "method": "comparative | absolute | hybrid"
        }
      },
      "m3:grammar_foundation:resolutionOrder": [
        "1. DomainSpecific benchmark  (M1 domain of the poclet)  <- DEFAULT",
        "2. CrossDomain benchmark     (adjacent M1 domain)",
        "3. Universal benchmark       (e.g. M0_AdaptiveImmuneResponse)",
        "4. Free scoring + justification                         <- last resort"
      ],
      "skos:note": "Philosophical grounding: Popper (falsifiability), Kuhn (paradigm shifts), Peirce (limit of inquiry). Mathematical grounding: norm-referenced measurement (Stevens 1946), inter-rater reliability (ICC, Cohen kappa)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:defeasibilityStatus",
      "@type": "owl:DatatypeProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "Defeasibility Status",
      "rdfs:comment": "Explicit declaration that a benchmark or canonical reference is provisional — valid until superseded by broader consensus. Makes revisability a first-class property of TSCG measurements.",
      "rdfs:range": {
        "@id": "xsd:string"
      },
      "skos:definition": "Defeasible knowledge: held as valid until defeated by stronger evidence or broader consensus. The normal epistemic status of scientific, legal, and practical knowledge.",
      "m3:grammar_foundation:structure": {
        "status": {
          "values": [
            "provisional",
            "established",
            "deprecated"
          ],
          "default": "provisional"
        },
        "validUntil": "superseded_by_better_consensus",
        "revisionTrigger": [
          "new_canonical_poclet_identified",
          "expert_consensus_challenged",
          "domain_expansion",
          "corpus_maturation"
        ]
      },
      "skos:note": "Analogous to stare decisis in law (precedent holds until overruled) and scientific paradigms (Kuhn: valid until anomalies accumulate)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:MonoidalType",
      "@type": "owl:Class",
      "rdfs:label": "Monoidal Type",
      "rdfs:comment": "Abstract class for all primitive types of the TSCG free monoidal grammars. Replaces former m3:M3Dimension (vestige of Hilbert-space / tensor formalism). Subclasses: types of Gt (ASFID — ×), types of Gm (REVOI — +), types of Gs (TKSL + poles: T, K, Ss, L, _^, _$ — |). A MonoidalType is a generator of the free monoid 𝕋* on 𝕋₀. Total: 16 primitives (Base16).",
      "skos:definition": "A generator of one of the three TSCG free monoidal grammars (Gt, Gm, Gs). MonoidalTypes are the atomic, irreducible elements from which all structural formula expressions are built via ×, +, and |.",
      "owl:equivalentClass": {
        "rdfs:comment": "Formerly named m3:M3Dimension — renamed to reflect Lambek/monoidal formalism"
      },
      "dcterms:created": "2026-05-20"
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:changelog",
      "@type": "owl:AnnotationProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "changelog",
      "rdfs:comment": "Ordered list of the most recent modifications to an ontology file, newest first. Declared in the apex ontology so that EVERY layer (M3, M2, M1, M0) can annotate its own owl:Ontology node without inverting the layer dependency: M2/M1/M0 all import M3, so m3:changelog is always a legal downward reference, whereas the former m2:changelog forced M3 files to depend on M2. RETENTION POLICY: the 3 most recent entries, except M3 files which keep up to 7 (rollback safety on the foundational layer). Declared as owl:AnnotationProperty rather than owl:DatatypeProperty because a changelog is documentation ABOUT the ontology, not an assertion about a domain entity \u2014 this keeps the corpus inside OWL DL. No rdfs:domain / rdfs:range axiom is asserted for the same reason; the intended domain is the owl:Ontology node.",
      "skos:note": "Aligned IN INTENT with adms:versionNotes (http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#versionNotes \u2014 'a description of changes between this version and the previous version of the Asset'). No rdfs:subPropertyOf axiom is asserted: m3:changelog is the CONTAINER (the ordered list of entries), whereas adms:versionNotes is the change text INSIDE each entry. DECISION (Michel, 2026-09-30, WS-1 lot 1c): ADMS is accepted as an external vocabulary; each entry is a node {owl:versionInfo, dcterms:date, adms:versionNotes}. The standard alternative (each entry as a version resource linked by dcterms:hasVersion) was considered and not retained: m3:changelog keeps its documented ordering, retention policy and annotation status.",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-07-22"
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:rationale",
      "@type": "owl:AnnotationProperty",
      "rdfs:label": "rationale",
      "rdfs:comment": "The reasoning that justifies a statement, an example or a design decision. Declared in the apex ontology because it is transversal (used in M2 and M3 files): a lower layer referencing m3: is a legal downward reference, whereas an m2: term inside an M3 file would invert the layer dependency.",
      "rdfs:subPropertyOf": {
        "@id": "skos:note"
      },
      "skos:note": "WS-1 lot 1g (Michel, 2026-09-30): no standard vocabulary (DCMI, SKOS, RDFS, OWL, ADMS, DCAT, schema.org) offers a rationale / justification property; SKOS only has generic notes. m3:rationale keeps the precise meaning while remaining machine-interpretable as a skos:note through rdfs:subPropertyOf (OWL 2 allows annotation-property hierarchies). Argumentation vocabularies such as IBIS model reasoning as a class structure and were judged too heavy for these free-text justifications.",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-09-30"
    },
    {
      "@id": "m3:grammar_foundation:ExternalVocabularyPolicy",
      "@type": "owl:NamedIndividual",
      "rdfs:label": "External vocabulary policy",
      "rdfs:comment": "How the TSCG corpus uses terms from external vocabularies. RULE 1 — every external term used anywhere in the Layer Cake (M3, M2, M1, M0) is DECLARED ONCE, here in the apex, with its OWL type and rdfs:isDefinedBy pointing to its source vocabulary; lower layers reach these declarations through the intra-Layer-Cake owl:imports chain. RULE 2 — external vocabularies are NEVER brought in by owl:imports: DCMI Terms, ADMS and schema.org type their terms as plain rdf:Property with range/domain axioms (e.g. dcterms:creator range dcterms:Agent) that conflict with the corpus' literal usage, and SKOS defines itself as an OWL Full ontology; importing them would push the corpus out of OWL 2 DL, whereas a local declaration keeps the official IRI (full interoperability) with a DL-safe typing chosen by TSCG. RULE 3 — the OWL 2 reserved vocabulary (IRIs with the rdf:, rdfs:, xsd: and owl: prefixes) is NOT declared, except the built-in annotation properties listed in OWL 2 Structural Specification §5.5 (rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, rdfs:isDefinedBy, owl:deprecated, owl:versionInfo, owl:priorVersion, owl:backwardCompatibleWith, owl:incompatibleWith), which are declared below when used. §5.1-§5.6 state that other reserved IRIs MUST NOT identify classes, properties or individuals in an OWL 2 DL ontology: the axiom vocabulary (rdf:type, rdfs:subClassOf, rdfs:subPropertyOf, rdfs:domain, rdfs:range, owl:imports, owl:inverseOf, owl:oneOf, owl:equivalentClass, the owl:Class / owl:*Property / owl:Ontology / owl:NamedIndividual types, …) is the language itself, explicitly defined by the OWL 2 and RDF specifications, not an implicit term. Consequently rdf:value (reserved, not a built-in annotation property) is not used; schema:value is used instead.",
      "skos:note": "DECISIONS (Michel, 2026-09-30, WS-1 lot 1h). Principle: everything must be interpretable by an RDF parser, no implicit term. D1: built-in annotation properties declared, reserved axiom vocabulary documented here and not declared (declaring it would leave OWL 2 DL and make reasoner results unreliable). D2: SKOS terms keep the typing published in the official SKOS RDF (semantic relations owl:ObjectProperty, skos:related also owl:SymmetricProperty, skos:notation owl:DatatypeProperty, notes and labels owl:AnnotationProperty, skos:Concept / skos:ConceptScheme owl:Class), with the official rdfs:subPropertyOf links restricted to terms the corpus uses; DCMI, ADMS and schema.org terms are owl:AnnotationProperty. D3: schema.org is ACCEPTED as an external vocabulary, used only where it fills a gap left by DCMI and SKOS, each term checked by meaning and typing, never by name. Accepted external vocabularies: DCMI Terms, SKOS, ADMS, schema.org. Measured by tscg_metrics.py gauges EXT-1 (standard term used but undeclared here, target 0) and EXT-2 (non-term in a standard namespace, target 0).",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-09-30"
    },
    {
